  "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"b10c\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"213\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/user_avatar/bnoc.xyz/b10c/48/4_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> b10c:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think this is looking at <strong>unrechable IPs</strong> in your addrman. Many nodes on e.g. AS3320 Deutsche Telekom are IPv4 home nodes that announce their IP, then after 24h rotate their IP, and announce a new one (I\u2019ve been working on a writeup of this). I think you should be explicit about this in your post.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks, yeah, this is misleading this is the new plot with reachable peers only.<br>\n<div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/original/1X/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff.png\" data-download-href=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff\" title=\"asmap_collapse\"><img src=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff_2_690x236.png\" alt=\"asmap_collapse\" data-base62-sha1=\"c19DUizFgZZGbvw50GS8sirZ0mz\" width=\"690\" height=\"236\" srcset=\"https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff_2_690x236.png, https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff_2_1035x354.png 1.5x, https://bnoc.xyz/uploads/default/optimized/1X/543b86ee19d13c655fe8a749cfe12cbed07146ff_2_1380x472.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"362026\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">asmap_collapse</span><span class=\"informations\">1520\u00d7520 116 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>",
